Documentation-Driven Testing (DDT) Platform Product Requirements Document
1. Project Overview and Strategic Objectives
1.1 Mission Statement
The mission of the Documentation-Driven Testing (DDT) platform is to transform OpenAPI specifications from passive documentation into autonomous, executable quality gates within a pure Crossplane and GitOps framework. By operationalizing the "Documentation as Contracts" paradigm, the platform ensures that API implementation never drifts from the documented source of truth, effectively treating the specification as the ultimate source of truth for both infrastructure and validation.
1.2 Target Audience
Platform Engineers: Architects designing automated quality gates, managing IaC lifecycles, and scaling GitOps promotion logic.
API Developers: Service owners requiring immediate, actionable feedback on API compliance and performance without manual test maintenance.
1.3 Key Value Propositions
89% Reduction in QA Effort: Eliminates manual test authorship by deriving validation rules, functional cases, and SLO checks directly from OpenAPI 3.0/3.1 specs.
40% Fewer Production Incidents: Dynamically identifies documentation drift and contract violations pre-merge, preventing breaking changes from reaching production.
Zero Operational Overhead: Tests are self-updating; any change to the specification in Git automatically triggers a re-generation of the quality gate.
Kubernetes-Native Enforcement: Seamlessly integrates with the Argo project suite and Crossplane, providing a closed-loop system for release gating.
