3. GitOps Promotion & Release Management
Promotion is governed by the GitOps Promoter toolset, which manages state transitions between environment branches.
3.1 Promotion Resources
PromotionStrategy: Configures the sequence of hydrated environment branches (e.g., dev -> stage -> prod). It defines the mandatory checks via activeCommitStatuses and proposedCommitStatuses.
ChangeTransferPolicy: Manages the pair-based logic between a "proposed" branch and a "live" branch. It autonomously manages the lifecycle of promotion Pull Requests.
3.2 Gating Mechanics: CommitStatus Integration
The CommitStatus CRD is the primary source of truth for promotion gates.
The Key Link: For a promotion to occur, the metadata.labels['promoter.argoproj.io/commit-status'] of a CommitStatus must match the keys defined in the PromotionStrategy (e.g., performance-test).
Autonomous Merging: The ChangeTransferPolicy will only merge a promotion PR if the CommitStatus phase for the specific Git SHA is success.
