5. Automated Workflow & Autonomous Gating
5.1 The Quality Gate Workflow
Upon a PR or commit, an Argo Workflow is triggered:
Execution: Runs DriveBy CLI using the flags derived from the KubeApp environment.
Reporting: Generates a JSON/Markdown report.
Status Propagation: The workflow creates/patches a CommitStatus CRD in the cluster.
5.2 Autonomous Status & Error Handling
The Workflow must interpret CLI exit codes to update the CommitStatus phase:
Exit Code 0 (Success): Sets CommitStatus phase to success. ChangeTransferPolicy merges the PR.
Exit Code 1 (Validation Failure): Sets CommitStatus phase to failure. Promotion is blocked; drift detected.
Exit Code 2 (Execution Error): Sets CommitStatus phase to failure. Indicates a breakdown in the test environment.
Exit Code 3 (Configuration Error): Triggers a Platform Failure alert. This indicates invalid CLI arguments (e.g., violating the Single-Method Auth rule) and requires Platform Engineer intervention.
