6. Security and Authentication Model
6.1 GitHub Authentication
The platform mandates GitHub App Authentication for SCM operations. This ensures granular, repository-specific permissions. The ProviderConfig for the GitHub provider must reference a Secret containing the appID, installationID, and the privateKey (PEM format).
6.2 API Authentication
The DriveBy engine enforces a Single Method validation rule. If more than one authentication method is configured via CLI flags, the tool will return Exit Code 3 and fail. This prevents ambiguous security contexts during validation.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
7. Observability and Feedback Loop
7.1 Developer Feedback
The platform provides direct feedback in the developer's workflow:
PR Comments: Using the --github-comment flag, the Markdown report is posted directly to the GitHub PR.
Commit Status: Visual pass/fail indicators appear in the GitHub UI, driven by the CommitStatus controller.
7.2 Resource Health & Reporting
Conditions: All KubeCore and Crossplane resources must expose .status.conditions. Platform health is monitored via the Ready and Synced types.
Artifacts: Validation reports (JSON/Markdown) must be archived by the Argo Workflow in the configured report-dir for historical drift analysis and auditability.